    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Enrich LinkedIn profiles in Google Sheets with Datacircle\n\n### Who's it for\nAnyone with LinkedIn profile URLs in a Google Sheet who wants each person's name, headline, location, company and title next to them.\n\n### How it works\nDatacircle is a data co-op. You send the provider's own request to api.datacircle.dev, with your Datacircle key. That's the only change. Right now we have 3 live LinkedIn profile APIs that we trust: Up2Data, HarvestAPI and Fetchin. Each request goes to the provider and gets the profile as it is today.\n\n1. The workflow reads each row's `linkedin_url` from your sheet.\n2. An HTTP Request node requests the profile from Up2Data, one URL a second.\n3. A Switch sends each answer down its branch: the profile, not found (free), not a profile URL (free), Up2Data's daily limit (the workflow then sends the same URL to HarvestAPI), or an error.\n4. Every branch writes the same columns back to the row.\n\n$2.375 per 1,000 through Up2Data (a profile it can't find is free), $3.70 per 1,000 through HarvestAPI. Up2Data takes $1 a day per account (421 profiles), with a shared daily limit for all customers, then answers 429 until 00:00 UTC. HarvestAPI has no daily limit.\n\n### Requirements\n- A Google Sheet with a `linkedin_url` column, and a Google Sheets credential.\n- A Datacircle API key. Sign up at datacircle.dev with your work email: a $5 credit, that's 2,105 LinkedIn profiles at $2.375 per 1,000. You send the profile's URL with your Datacircle key: no LinkedIn login, no cookies, no browser.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Add a **Header Auth** credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `Token `, then your key. Pick it on both HTTP Request nodes.\n2. Pick your sheet in **Read LinkedIn URLs** and **Write the columns**.\n3. Run the workflow.\n\n### How to customize\nSwap Google Sheets for Airtable or your CRM: any node whose items have a `linkedin_url`. Every field we return: https://docs.datacircle.dev/linkedin-profile. A call your balance can't cover answers 402. Add funds, from $5, on your dashboard.",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 560
      },
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -160
      ],
      "id": "58ed3c81-fbf3-45f1-af6a-4b28711f593d"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Your sheet\nPick your sheet in **Read LinkedIn URLs**. Each row needs a `linkedin_url`, like `https://www.linkedin.com/in/williamhgates`.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        120
      ],
      "id": "57d3c943-a659-4a92-aef1-d7db4b3a7b51"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. The call\nUp2Data through Datacircle, one URL a second. Pick your **Header Auth** credential here and on **HarvestAPI**: Name `Authorization`, Value `Token `, then your key.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        380,
        120
      ],
      "id": "8552b2af-3efa-4c2b-af34-9f6a2d77143b"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Each answer\n200: the profile. 422: private or deleted, free. 400: not a profile URL, free. 429: Up2Data's daily limit, so the same URL goes to HarvestAPI. Anything else: the status and the reason.",
        "height": 980,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        840,
        -120
      ],
      "id": "9441df19-7e30-4401-8253-95867b664b90"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 4. Back to your sheet\nEvery branch has the same columns. The row is updated by its `linkedin_url`; a column the sheet doesn't have yet is added.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1340,
        120
      ],
      "id": "7157b47a-178d-42ce-aa30-336e21a33584"
